    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen I exit neovim inside [tmux control mode](https://github.com/tmux/tmux/wiki/Control-Mode) session (started from `tmux -CC`), it will leave (which I assume to be) control code in the terminal, see this asciinema recording: https://asciinema.org/a/79diizut3ozwB6ON\n\nI confirmed this in 2 terminals supporting tmux control mode: WezTerm nightly, and ChromeOS's default terminal.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```\ntmux -CC\nnvim\n:q\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nExit cleanly\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.12.3\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, vim 9.2.858\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux Debian testing\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nwezterm nightly, chromos terminal\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nscreen-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nDebian official apt server",
