        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Finished bisecting to 646a8f663e23d641f5ae653847dcbd2ab172f859, which is where the DA1 I referenced in `terminfo_disable` was added. However, it's still not an nvim issue IMO. We send out a DA1 request and get two DA1 responses. Whether that's tmux's or WezTerm's issue, I don't know, but that's the cause of the problem. We should only get back one response. It works in iTerm under `tmux -CC`, so my best guess at present is WezTerm.",
